02:09:06,070 --> 02:09:09,290
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: Patungkol po sa Special Education Fund,

2523
02:09:10,070 --> 02:09:13,470
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: diba meron po dito yung mga lungsod, yung mga probinsya.

2524
02:09:14,130 --> 02:09:17,190
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: At sa tingin ko, several billions of pesos po ito.

2525
02:09:17,430 --> 02:09:19,110
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: Kapag sinumada mo.

2526
02:09:19,350 --> 02:09:19,750
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ano yun?

2527
02:09:22,750 --> 02:09:24,750
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: Meron namang guidelines na naipalabas.

2528
02:09:25,530 --> 02:09:29,910
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: Pero ang tanong ko, yung gamit po ba nito, ay nasusubaybayan ba yan?

2529
02:09:30,090 --> 02:09:31,430
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: Sa Department of Education.

2530
02:09:31,670 --> 02:09:35,150
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: Kasi sa tingin ko, yung paggamit po ng Special Education Fund,

2531
02:09:35,570 --> 02:09:41,530
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: kinakailangang naka-align po yun sa programs and projects ng Department of Education.

2532
02:09:41,530 --> 02:09:50,670
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: At tinitingnan dapat kung paano ito nakakatulong sa goals, objective ng Department of Education.

2533
02:09:51,670 --> 02:09:59,850
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At tama po kayo, Your Honor, na mahalaga yung SCF at dapat naka-align yun sa mga layunin ng DepEd.

2534
02:10:00,090 --> 02:10:03,310
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But unfortunately, there's such a thing as local autonomy, diba?

2535
02:10:03,450 --> 02:10:06,310
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So mixed experiences ang DepEd ho dyan.

2536
02:10:06,730 --> 02:10:12,010
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pag medyo forward-looking at enlightened yung local chief executive,

2537
02:10:12,770 --> 02:10:17,870
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: pinapaubayan na po sa DepEd ang paggamit po ng Special Education Fund.

2538
02:10:17,870 --> 02:10:22,590
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pero having said that, pinalawak na po natin yung menu ng Special Education Fund

2539
02:10:22,590 --> 02:10:26,490
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: para hindi lang yung traditional items ang pwedeng pondohan.

2540
02:10:27,070 --> 02:10:29,870
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: But again, yung talagang coercive

2541
02:10:30,090 --> 02:10:33,030
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: power over the use of the SEF is not with DepEd.

2542
02:10:33,150 --> 02:10:35,950
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: It's probably with DOF if it lies with any agency.

2543
02:10:36,170 --> 02:10:38,310
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kasi hindi naman kami yung nagpamonitor doon.

2544
02:10:39,010 --> 02:10:46,470
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: At yung ibang, I'm aware that some LGUs, yung SCF allotment for that year,

2545
02:10:46,570 --> 02:10:48,630
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: hindi nila ginagastos, minsan iniipon po nila yun.

2546
02:10:49,830 --> 02:10:51,250
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: Yun lang po, Madam Chairman.

2547
02:10:51,250 --> 02:10:56,250
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: At muli, yung pagpapayag po ng suporta sa Department of Education,

2548
02:10:57,090 --> 02:10:59,970
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: including the request for additional budget.

2549
02:11:00,090 --> 02:11:02,510
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: Yes, sir. Thank you.

2550
02:11:02,610 --> 02:11:03,190
Rep. Nelson S. Legacion: Thank you very much.

2551
02:11:03,190 --> 02:11:06,110
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Maraming-maraming salamat, Kong Nelson, at mabuhay po kayo.

2552
02:11:06,170 --> 02:11:07,090
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Diyos mabalas. Thank you.

2553
02:11:10,490 --> 02:11:15,890
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Before we go on lunch break, I will recognize one more,

2554
02:11:16,050 --> 02:11:22,870
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: and then we go to lunch break and toilet break as well with the Secretary.

2555
02:11:23,130 --> 02:11:23,310
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: Okay.

2556
02:11:23,830 --> 02:11:28,230
Rep. Maria Carmen S. Zamora: The Chair now recognizes Representative Sarah Elago.

2557
02:11:29,370 --> 02:11:31,050
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maraming salamat, Madam Chair.

2558
02:11:31,350 --> 02:11:32,430
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Magandang araw.

2559
02:11:32,490 --> 02:11:36,970
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: As a DepEd family, tungkol sa implementation ng Bawal Bastos Law,

2560
02:11:37,470 --> 02:11:43,490
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ang programa at activities para rito ay kinukuha mula sa Learner Rights and Protection Funds,

2561
02:11:43,630 --> 02:11:45,910
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: pati na rin sa Gender and Development Budget.

2562
02:11:46,450 --> 02:11:52,170
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Nagawa na po ba lahat ng ating regional offices ang kanya-kanyang mga code of conduct and consultation?

2563
02:11:52,770 --> 02:11:59,630
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At lahat ba ng divisions at schools ay may funksional na Committee on Decorum and Investigation?

2564
02:12:17,200 --> 02:12:19,500
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Your Honor, they're still in the process of completing.

2565
02:12:19,500 --> 02:12:26,260
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: The plans that you mentioned, Your Honor, the budget is subsumed under the Gender and Development portion of the DepEd budget, Your Honor.

2566
02:12:27,340 --> 02:12:30,180
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We can submit a report per region, Your Honor.

2567
02:12:31,100 --> 02:12:32,860
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Maraming salamat, Madam Chair.

2568
02:12:32,980 --> 02:12:37,240
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Abukad sa mismo report ng Bawal Bastos Law implementation,

2569
02:12:37,740 --> 02:12:44,380
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: nais din natin makuha kung magkano rin yung nagagastos para sa mga referral at intervention programs,

2570
02:12:44,380 --> 02:12:47,380
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: lalo na sa mental health, psychosocial support services,

2571
02:12:47,940 --> 02:12:52,540
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para sa mga victim-survivors of sexual violence.

2572
02:12:52,700 --> 02:12:55,320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Hindi lang po ito para sa mga estudyante, Madam Chair.

2573
02:12:55,700 --> 02:13:01,320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Pero maski ho ang mga guro at ibang mga non-teaching personnel at lahat ng education stakeholders

2574
02:13:01,320 --> 02:13:06,720
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ay kailangan nakaka-access ng ganitong mahalagang mga servisyo.

2575
02:13:06,800 --> 02:13:13,980
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman, Madam Chair, nais kong magtanong tungkol sa policy ng DepEd tungkol sa class suspension.

2576
02:13:13,980 --> 02:13:16,340
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Dahil ngayon, sunod-sunod ang bagyo.

2577
02:13:16,700 --> 02:13:17,900
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: May habagat na may dalang

2578
02:13:17,940 --> 02:13:21,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: malakas na pag-ulan, nandiyan ang epekto ng pagbaha,

2579
02:13:22,000 --> 02:13:26,260
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: nandyan din ang bantanang super el nino at extreme heat.

2580
02:13:26,520 --> 02:13:33,220
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At ang risulta nito, dumarami at sunod-sunod ang bilang ng nawawalang school days dahil sa class suspension.

2581
02:13:33,860 --> 02:13:37,640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: May development na huba kung paano ma-address ng DepEd

2582
02:13:37,640 --> 02:13:42,460
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: yung mga concerns ng ating kababayan tungkol sa mga late na class suspension.

2583
02:13:42,460 --> 02:13:47,260
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: May pondo bang ilalaan para sa catch-up programs, make-up classes,

2584
02:13:47,940 --> 02:13:52,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: paano namu-monitor at natitiyak na effective ang mga programa na ito?

2585
02:13:53,700 --> 02:13:56,060
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Thank you, Madam Chair, Your Honor.

2586
02:13:57,560 --> 02:14:02,640
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Meron po tayong draft EO to amend the existing EO 66.

2587
02:14:04,360 --> 02:14:11,160
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, in-approve na po nung SDC or Social Development Committee of DepDev.

2588
02:14:11,260 --> 02:14:12,280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: That was last week lang.

2589
02:14:12,280 --> 02:14:16,460
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And ang highlights nun, yung nabanggit nyo,

2590
02:14:16,460 --> 02:14:22,660
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: yung kasi dati, ano lang eh, weather hazard, rain and wind hazard lang ho.

2591
02:14:23,120 --> 02:14:24,720
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ngayon, kasama na ho yung earthquake.

2592
02:14:25,100 --> 02:14:32,220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, may automatic suspensions for pag yung air quality is based on the limits that DNR sets,

2593
02:14:32,740 --> 02:14:40,280
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: yung earthquake, certain earthquake level, tapos may pag-asa levels for heat index din po.

2594
02:14:40,660 --> 02:14:41,840
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, sinama na ho natin yun.

2595
02:14:42,220 --> 02:14:44,220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, yung hazards na expand po yung menu.

2596
02:14:44,220 --> 02:14:46,220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And we have such...

2597
02:14:46,460 --> 02:14:51,860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: We're developing this new concept called the granular suspension and resumption of class, ma'am.

2598
02:14:52,120 --> 02:14:53,320
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Anong ibig sabihin ito?

2599
02:14:53,880 --> 02:14:58,700
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Kapag kasi sa ngayon, meron tayong automatic suspension sa national level or sa provincial levels.

2600
02:14:58,700 --> 02:14:59,700
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pagka...

2601
02:15:00,000 --> 02:15:03,740
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: yung certain color index ng ulan.

2602
02:15:04,640 --> 02:15:06,100
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Tapos meron din tayong local suspension

2603
02:15:06,100 --> 02:15:08,440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: at the level of the governor, the mayors.

2604
02:15:08,960 --> 02:15:12,240
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So ngayon, meron ho kasing ang naging feedback ho sa amin

2605
02:15:12,240 --> 02:15:16,380
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: in our consultations is yung mga ibang skwelahan

2606
02:15:16,380 --> 02:15:19,080
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: na sakop doon mga suspension na nabanggit,

2607
02:15:19,500 --> 02:15:21,860
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: eh hindi naman sila lahat apektado.

2608
02:15:22,040 --> 02:15:24,220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Ibig sabihin, nag-declare si governor dito,

2609
02:15:24,740 --> 02:15:27,220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: eh itong sityo na ito, ito yung barangay,

2610
02:15:27,220 --> 02:15:28,960
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: hindi pala umuulan doon sa lugar nila.

2611
02:15:28,960 --> 02:15:31,440
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So we're under this new draft EO,

2612
02:15:31,820 --> 02:15:33,000
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: which will be

2613
02:15:33,220 --> 02:15:35,600
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: hopefully approved by the president in the coming weeks.

2614
02:15:36,840 --> 02:15:39,840
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Pwede na pong mag-resume with coordination

2615
02:15:39,840 --> 02:15:41,520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: with the local chief executives,

2616
02:15:41,940 --> 02:15:44,360
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: ang ating mga public and private schools, Your Honor,

2617
02:15:44,500 --> 02:15:47,080
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: para ma-minimize na nga yung learning loss.

2618
02:15:48,720 --> 02:15:52,580
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: And really, tama ho kayo because this is a very relevant topic

2619
02:15:52,580 --> 02:15:55,140
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: given the effects of El Nino,

2620
02:15:55,360 --> 02:15:56,520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: the effects of climate change,

2621
02:15:56,520 --> 02:15:58,400
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: yung haze mula sa Indonesia,

2622
02:15:58,400 --> 02:16:01,220
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: talagang unprecedented po yung weather disturbances

2623
02:16:01,220 --> 02:16:03,520
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: that we're seeing at present, Your Honor.

2624
02:16:04,720 --> 02:16:07,400
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Madam Chair, sa nabanggit na halimbawa ng ating Secretary,

2625
02:16:08,440 --> 02:16:10,900
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: sa kabilang banda, mayroon din mga kaso na

2626
02:16:10,900 --> 02:16:14,040
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: hindi affected yung eskwelahan,

2627
02:16:14,220 --> 02:16:16,880
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: pero yung mga estudyante sa mga lugar na binaha

2628
02:16:16,880 --> 02:16:18,620
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: o sa mga lugar na affected,

2629
02:16:19,020 --> 02:16:21,760
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ay may nararanasan na pagbaha

2630
02:16:21,760 --> 02:16:24,840
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: at iba't iba pong kahirapan sa pagpapasok.

2631
02:16:24,960 --> 02:16:27,100
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kaya dapat may isang ala-alang rin ito.

2632
02:16:27,100 --> 02:16:28,320
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman, Madam Chair,

2633
02:16:28,400 --> 02:16:30,600
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: may podo ba para sa dagdag allowance

2634
02:16:30,600 --> 02:16:33,300
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para sa home-based work ng mga guro?

2635
02:16:33,460 --> 02:16:35,400
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kasi ho, diba, ang karaniwan na nangyayari

2636
02:16:35,920 --> 02:16:37,160
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: pag may class suspension,

2637
02:16:37,420 --> 02:16:41,640
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: sila ho ay nagkakandak na kanilang klase

2638
02:16:41,640 --> 02:16:44,680
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: mula sa kanilang bahay through online means.

2639
02:16:44,820 --> 02:16:46,300
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Meron po bang dagdag na allowance

2640
02:16:46,300 --> 02:16:48,080
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para sa home-based work na ito?

2641
02:16:50,150 --> 02:16:51,510
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Wala po for home-based work,

2642
02:16:51,650 --> 02:16:54,110
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: pero tama ho kayo, dapat maging flexible ho tayo

2643
02:16:54,110 --> 02:16:56,250
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: dahil maaring yung eskwelahan hindi apektado,

2644
02:16:56,410 --> 02:16:59,350
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: pero yung estudyante o yung guro ay apektado

2645
02:16:59,350 --> 02:17:01,650
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: dahil nakatira sila sa ibang lugar.

2646
02:17:01,810 --> 02:17:04,130
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, we'll make allowance for that, Your Honor,

2647
02:17:04,270 --> 02:17:07,970
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: dun sa allowing certain students

2648
02:17:07,970 --> 02:17:10,190
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: to be excused from attending school

2649
02:17:10,190 --> 02:17:11,970
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: during those times

2650
02:17:11,970 --> 02:17:14,330
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: and using alternative delivery means

2651
02:17:14,330 --> 02:17:15,170
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: na lang or modes

2652
02:17:15,170 --> 02:17:18,690
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: dito sa kanilang mga estudyante na apektado,

2653
02:17:18,790 --> 02:17:19,030
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Your Honor.

2654
02:17:19,570 --> 02:17:21,850
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Madam Chair, bukod po dun sa allowance,

2655
02:17:21,950 --> 02:17:23,930
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: dagdag na allowance para sa home-based work

2656
02:17:23,930 --> 02:17:24,870
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ng mga teachers,

2657
02:17:25,790 --> 02:17:27,050
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: nire-raise ko rin po yung concern.

2658
02:17:27,050 --> 02:17:28,990
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Halimbawa, yung mga laptop na,

2659
02:17:29,350 --> 02:17:30,590
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: provided for teachers,

2660
02:17:30,950 --> 02:17:33,350
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: magagamit lang nila mismo dun sa school premises

2661
02:17:33,350 --> 02:17:36,010
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: at hindi po sila pinapayagan na maiuwi.

2662
02:17:36,350 --> 02:17:38,350
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Gayun din po yung concern ng ilan na

2663
02:17:38,350 --> 02:17:40,350
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: hindi naman lahat ay makakashift

2664
02:17:40,350 --> 02:17:42,250
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: agad-agad sa online means.

2665
02:17:42,370 --> 02:17:43,970
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Halimbawa, pag wala hong kuryente,

2666
02:17:44,130 --> 02:17:45,470
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: walang internet services,

2667
02:17:45,870 --> 02:17:48,010
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: sana po, maisang alang-alang ito ng DepEd.

2668
02:17:48,270 --> 02:17:50,210
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon naman, tungkol, Madam Chair,

2669
02:17:50,310 --> 02:17:54,930
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: dun sa pagpapatupad ng DepEd Order No. 32,

2670
02:17:55,470 --> 02:17:57,750
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: this particular order mandates DepEd

2671
02:17:57,750 --> 02:17:58,870
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: to uphold human rights,

2672
02:17:58,990 --> 02:17:59,330
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: peace-building,

2673
02:17:59,350 --> 02:18:01,350
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: and child protection in all educational spaces,

2674
02:18:02,610 --> 02:18:05,030
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: particularly the use of school premises

2675
02:18:05,030 --> 02:18:07,510
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: by the military for civic action,

2676
02:18:07,610 --> 02:18:09,230
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: including medical and dental missions,

2677
02:18:09,410 --> 02:18:11,390
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: symposia, and other public service activities

2678
02:18:11,390 --> 02:18:14,090
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: is prohibited unless in response

2679
02:18:14,090 --> 02:18:16,030
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: to natural disasters or emergencies

2680
02:18:16,030 --> 02:18:18,890
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: where civil authorities require such assistance.

2681
02:18:19,690 --> 02:18:21,710
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Ngayon po ba may pondo kayo

2682
02:18:21,710 --> 02:18:23,350
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: para sa pagpapatupad nito?

2683
02:18:24,090 --> 02:18:26,450
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: At meron ba kayong active na mechanism

2684
02:18:26,450 --> 02:18:29,250
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: for monitoring, evaluation, investigation?

2685
02:18:29,350 --> 02:18:31,050
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Hanggang sa pagpapanagot

2686
02:18:31,050 --> 02:18:32,490
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ng mga lumalabag nito?

2687
02:18:33,850 --> 02:18:35,610
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Anong sanction pag lumabag?

2688
02:18:37,410 --> 02:18:39,750
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Well, nirirespeto naman, by and large,

2689
02:18:39,830 --> 02:18:41,150
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: nirirespeto naman ho yung

2690
02:18:41,150 --> 02:18:42,630
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: ganong limitasyon.

2691
02:18:42,770 --> 02:18:44,170
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Para naging tradisyon na rin ho yun

2692
02:18:44,170 --> 02:18:46,750
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: na yung mga armed services ay

2693
02:18:46,750 --> 02:18:48,830
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: hanggang gate lang po ng paaralan.

2694
02:18:49,450 --> 02:18:51,710
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: So, I think the exceptions is

2695
02:18:51,710 --> 02:18:53,410
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: yung pag nagkaroon ng shooting

2696
02:18:53,410 --> 02:18:55,350
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: at knifing

2697
02:18:56,030 --> 02:18:58,470
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: or other security incidents,

2698
02:18:58,470 --> 02:18:58,870
DepEd Secretary Sonny Angara: Your Honor.

2699
02:18:59,350 --> 02:19:01,090
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: May mga reports, Madam Chair,

2700
02:19:01,170 --> 02:19:02,350
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: sa representation na ito

2701
02:19:02,350 --> 02:19:03,610
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na sa mga learning tools

2702
02:19:03,610 --> 02:19:08,920
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: na papahawak yung mga bata

2703
02:19:08,920 --> 02:19:11,740
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: ng mga baril.

2704
02:19:11,860 --> 02:19:13,780
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: Kahit pa ito ay walang laman na bala

2705
02:19:13,780 --> 02:19:14,620
Rep. Sarah Jane I. Elago: o kung anuman,

2706
02:19:15,120 --> 02:19:17,240
